{
  "id": "pokemon-card-trainers-magazine",
  "name": "Pokémon Card Trainers Magazine",
  "category": "publication_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon Card Trainers was Media Factory's official card game magazine, published from 1999 until early 2003 and sent to members of the Pokémon Card Fan Club as part of their membership; the first issue, in May 1999, launched the club. Its first card, a Pikachu from a photo in the Nintendo 64 game Pokémon Snap, was peeled from an insert sheet; later bonus cards came sealed in their own packets: Dr. Ooyama's bilingual Exeggutor, the Neo Genesis Darkness Energy two months before that set came out, Murkrow, Steelix in cosmos holo, Smeargle, Unown [J], Misdreavus, and Dark Ivysaur and Dark Venusaur with the \"GB\" mark of the Game Boy promos. Vol. 3 also drew ten readers for the Tropical Wind card of the 1999 Tropical Mega Battle, and Vol. 17 had a voucher for two Touch Generation Change! cards at Battle Road in summer 2002.\n\nFrom 2001 the cards were numbered promos: Rocket's Scizor, Celebi and Bill among the P promos, and after the magazine was relaunched with Vol. 14 in January 2002, now six issues a year, three T promos with each issue, 001/T to 024/T. They came in families: the Eeveelutions, the Slowpoke family, the middle stages of the Johto and then the Kanto starters, Midori Harada's legendary birds in one picture across three cards, the Dratini line, the Larvitar line, and Imakuni?'s Whismur, Loudred and Exploud ex with the last issue, Vol. 21 of March 2003. Many of the magazine's cards came in English with the same art as Black Star, Best of Game or POP Series promos.",
